{"title":"2011 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let X and Y be the following sums of arithmetic sequences: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525b936d5ed2de6f87450939c587d6421b133c9f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}X &amp;=&amp; 10+12+14+\\cdots+100,\\\\ Y &amp;=&amp; 12+14+16+\\cdots+102.\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"259\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/49659cb7aa29cc0ed1e7ca802e9037dd62ae6b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y - X?$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87dd3ff550e21b204ae29bc075bfa777ac80ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 92\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 98\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 100\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 102\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 112$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that both sequences have equal numbers of terms, so reformat the sequence to look like: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516f2a749ff4b6f07dce34b743b20906e35d5a8b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} Y = \\ &amp;12 + 14 + \\cdots + 100 + 102\\\\ X = 10 \\ + \\ &amp;12 +  14 + \\cdots + 100\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"284\" height=\"39\" />\nFrom here it is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b5dd30c641685971ccc4289466179054d75cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y - X = 102 - 10 = \\boxed{92 \\ \\mathbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"235\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Another way to see this is to let the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f65d44832034a8684bc6b52de4719b38af55ea0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12+14+16+...+100=x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"224\" height=\"14\" /> So, the sequences become\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/056cf14cc08dfcec6b8fdd0056959ca23b47a797.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} X = 10+x \\\\ Y= x+102 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"98\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Like before, the difference between the two sequences is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf1c65720b691dcdc08d7c93ecb3196ba36ce43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y-X=102-12=92.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"191\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that every number in Y's sequence is two more than every corresponding number in X's sequence. Since there are 46 numbers in each sequence, the difference must be\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/a/70aadaf39344d9338919559332c34408263fbaba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46\\cdot 2=\\boxed{92}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72c8e402779724fbec8e8ab70af2a5c9b2b932fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} X&amp;=10+12+14+\\cdots +100 \\\\ Y&amp;=X-10+102 = X+92 \\\\  Y-X &amp;= (X+92)-X \\\\      &amp;= \\boxed{92} \\quad \\quad \\textbf{(A)}\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"268\" height=\"98\" />\n</p><p><br />\n- <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4b2b4ed349c1e7a071b605ce366b4b66c81866f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{herobrine-india}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"109\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In an actual contest, this would probably take too much time but is nevertheless a solution.\nThe general formula for computing sums of any arithmetic sequence where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of terms, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is the first term and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> is the last term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f878d096d91325a51ac90605a2eb94db7a393d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(f+l)x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"40\" />. If one uses that formula for both sequences, they will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfb507c509c214ee49e59d42ab1302577243273f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2530$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> as the sum for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e0937bab45c1ce6579c2e994849a39390c5590b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2622$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> as the sum for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\nSubtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, one will get the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25689a03c59a454f439e536518f59e2248895db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{92 \\text{\\textbf{ (A)}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n- danfan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/L6utIF9FzPQ\">https://youtu.be/L6utIF9FzPQ</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=biR0pgefTCs&amp;t=2s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=biR0pgefTCs&amp;t=2s</a>\n</p><p>~piHard\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A\">2011 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Prob